    "Let me check the changelog section to add a documentation entry consistent with repo conventions.",
    "Let me review the final diff and clean up scratch files.",
    "**Summary of the fix**\n\nRoot cause: `Command.make_context()` used `ctx.scope(cleanup=False)` while parsing. When an eager option's callback called `ctx.exit()`, the resulting `Exit` propagated out of `make_context` before `main()`'s `with self.make_context(...) as ctx:` could be entered, so `Context.close()` never ran and every `call_on_close` callback registered by earlier eager options was dropped.\n\nChange in `src/click/core.py` (`Command.make_context`): wrap `self.parse_args(ctx, args)` so that on any exception (including `ctx.exit()`'s `Exit`) the context is closed before the exception propagates. `ctx.close()` is invoked *inside* the scope, before the context is popped, preserving the existing \"close before pop\" guarantee that callbacks can still see the context as the current one.\n\nResulting behaviour matches the requirements:\n- `--register --force-exit` \u2192 both cleanups run (LIFO: exiting option's, then earlier option's).\n- `--force-exit --register` \u2192 only the exiting option's cleanup runs, since the later eager option is never processed.\n\nTests added to `tests/test_context.py`:\n- `test_call_on_close_runs_when_eager_option_exits`\n- `test_call_on_close_skipped_after_eager_exit`\n- `test_call_on_close_resets_state_after_eager_exit` (the global-logger-level leak)\n\nAll three fail against the unfixed source and pass with the fix. Full suite: 606 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed. (Note: under this checkout's pytest 9.1.1 with the repo's `filterwarnings = [\"error\"]`, `tests/test_basic.py` fails at collection on a pre-existing `PytestRemovedIn10Warning` about parametrize iterables \u2014 unrelated to this change; running with `-o filterwarnings=ignore` collects and passes everything.)\n\nDONE"
   ],
