    "Clean up scratch files and add a changelog entry:",
    "Let me verify regular exceptions during parsing also trigger cleanup (same root cause) and that the command body's callbacks are unaffected:",
    "The fix is complete and verified.\n\n**Root cause:** Eager option callbacks run inside `Command.make_context`, which parses args within `ctx.scope(cleanup=False)` to defer close-callback cleanup until after the command body. When an eager callback raised `Exit` (via `ctx.exit()`), parsing aborted, `make_context` never returned, and `main`'s `with ctx:` was never entered \u2014 so `ctx.close()` never ran and the `ExitStack` callbacks leaked.\n\n**Fix (`src/click/core.py`):** In `make_context`, wrap `parse_args` and call `ctx.close()` if parsing fails, before the exception propagates. The close happens while the context is still on the stack (before pop), preserving `test_close_before_pop` semantics.\n\n**Result:**\n- `--option-with-callback --force-exit` \u2192 both cleanups run: `[\"a\", \"b\", \"close b\", \"close a\"]`\n- `--force-exit --option-with-callback` \u2192 only the exiting option's cleanup: `[\"b\", \"close b\"]`\n- The logger-level case no longer leaks (level reset on exit).\n\n**Tests:** Added `test_call_on_close_eager_exit` (both orderings) and `test_call_on_close_eager_exit_does_not_leak_state` (logger state) to `tests/test_context.py`, plus a `CHANGES.rst` entry. Full suite: 605 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\nDONE"
