    "Root cause and fix:\n\nIn `Option.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), the automatic `flag_value` inference (`flag_value = not self.default`) was nested inside the `if is_flag and type is None:` branch. Per changelog PR 2829, that inference must apply whenever `is_flag` is true and no explicit `flag_value` was given. With an explicit `type=`, `flag_value` stayed `None`, so `add_to_parser` used `const=None`; the parser stored `None`, and `consume_value`/`process_value` cast it through the declared type (`bool` \u2192 `False`, `str` \u2192 `\"None\"`, `int` \u2192 `None`). Hoisting the inference out of the `type is None` block fixes it while leaving type-guessing unchanged.\n\nVerified behaviour after the fix:\n- `type=bool`, `--foo` \u2192 `True`; omitted \u2192 `False`\n- `type=bool, default=True`, `--foo` \u2192 `False`; omitted \u2192 `True`\n- `type=click.BOOL`, `--foo` \u2192 `True`\n- `type=str`, `--foo` \u2192 `\"True\"`\n\nTests: added `test_flag_value_inferred_with_explicit_type` and parametrized `test_is_flag_with_explicit_type` to `tests/test_options.py` (7 cases); all fail before the fix and pass after. Full suite: 726 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed (the `tests/test_basic.py` collection error is a pre-existing pytest-10 deprecation unrelated to this change).\n\nDONE"
