    "The tests fail before the fix and pass after. Let me clean up the scratch file and run the full suite one more time.",
    "Let me do a final check using `click.echo` directly to match the report's phrasing, and confirm the cleanup:",
    "The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `Option.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), the default `flag_value` was derived from the option's default **inside** the `if is_flag and type is None:` branch:\n\n```python\nif is_flag and type is None:\n    if flag_value is None:\n        flag_value = not self.default   # \u2190 only ran when no explicit type\n    self.type = types.convert_type(None, flag_value)\n```\n\nWhen an explicit `type=` was supplied, that branch was skipped, leaving `flag_value = None`. The parser then registered the flag with `const=None`, so activating `--foo` fed `None` through the type conversion \u2014 yielding `False` for `bool`, `\"None\"`/empty for `str`, etc.\n\n## Fix\n\nSet `flag_value` independently of the type, and only infer the type when `type` was omitted:\n\n```python\nif is_flag and flag_value is None:\n    flag_value = not self.default\n\nself.type: types.ParamType\nif is_flag and type is None:\n    self.type = types.convert_type(None, flag_value)\n```\n\nThis preserves the existing rule that `flag_value` is only defaulted when `is_flag` is true (per CHANGES pr 2829), and leaves non-flag/optional-value options untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n`--foo` now yields `True` for `type=bool`/`click.BOOL`, `False` for `type=bool, default=True`, and `\"True\"` for `type=str`; omitting the flag is unchanged in every case.\n\nTests added to `tests/test_options.py`:\n- `test_flag_with_explicit_type` \u2014 parametrized CliRunner cases over the reported declarations (passed/omitted).\n- `test_flag_value_is_set_with_explicit_type` \u2014 asserts `flag_value` is derived from the default for `bool`/`click.BOOL`/`str`/`int`.\n\nBoth new tests fail against the unfixed source and pass after. Full suite: **730 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed**. No unrelated behavior changed.\n\nDONE"
